; ======================================================================
;  #CAP_MMC = 0 - AND THE CARD WORKS. This group is the RAW BLOCK family:
;  `mmc read`, `mmc write`, sector counts. The card is reached instead
;  through the storage and file seams, which is a different question and
;  a different command set.
;
;  It is 0 rather than 1 because the raw family's contract includes
;  things this board's driver deliberately refuses - an unrestricted
;  write, for one. RaspberryPi3/Lib/sdhost.pbi will only write inside a
;  window somebody declared, because the card carries the immutable
;  loader and both A/B slots, and `mmc write 0` on the boot card is a
;  board that stops booting. Offering the family and then refusing half
;  of it would be worse than not offering it.
; ======================================================================

Procedure.i HwMmcUp()
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure
Procedure.i HwMmcBlockCount()
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure
Procedure.i HwMmcBlockSize()
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure
Procedure.i HwMmcCanWrite()
